# The backend image builds from the REPO ROOT (it needs data/seed/), so without this
# file Docker ships the entire tree — including the 205 MB Dataset/ directory — to the
# daemon on every build. On Render that is a slow build at best and a failed one at worst.

# Raw vendor datasets. Only the build_*_seed.py authoring scripts read these, and they
# run locally, never in the image. The built catalogue in data/seed/ is what ships.
Dataset/

# Dependencies and build output
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
venv/
frontend/dist/
frontend/dev-dist/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Caches
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
**/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
htmlcov/
.coverage

# Local databases — these hold demo credentials
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite3

# Secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# VCS, docs, and tooling that the runtime does not need
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
docs/
graphify-out/
_bmad/
_bmad-output/
.agent/
.agents/
README.md
NOTICE.md
**/*.md

# Frontend source: the API image has no use for it
frontend/
